WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.320
Looking for a thrilling movie night, but stuck
on what to watch?

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:07.980
Don't worry, Netflix is jam-packed with great
thrillers that'll send a chill up your spine.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.150
From criminally overlooked heist flicks to
gritty, hard-boiled revenge tales, here are

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.080
all the best thrillers on Netflix that nobody
seems to be talking about.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.830
Small Crimes

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:23.890
Directed by Evan Katz, 2017's Small Crimes
takes Jaime Lannister out of Westeros and

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.210
sticks him in the middle of small town America.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:31.099
Played by Nikolaj Coster-Waldau, Joe Denton
is a corrupt cop recently released from prison

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:33.120
after carving up the local DA.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.690
Now that he's a free man, this alcoholic narcissist
is trapped in limbo, with everyone giving

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:38.820
him the evil eye.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.940
His mom is pressuring him to clean up his
life, his wife and kids won't talk to him,

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.070
and random strangers are trying to bash his
head in.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.320
E across
Worse still, a sleazy police lieutenant wants

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:51.150
Joe to take out a dying gangster to make sure
the mobster doesn't squeal on all the dirty

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.190
cops in town.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.830
But really, this is a movie that defies plot
description, as Small Crimes delves into some

00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:01.780
twisty plotlines involving prostitution, drunken
soldiers, and a deranged gangster with his

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.500
own personal torture dungeon.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.740
Coster-Waldau is at his best here, and this
complicated plot unfolds with a gut-punch

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.990
of a final showdown, one that will leave you
looking at the deadbeat protagonist in a completely

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:12.990
different light.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:17.000
Despite all the twists and turns, Small Crimes
is ultimately a movie about forgiveness and

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.110
whether or not we deserve it.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.630
The Crying Game

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:25.341
Directed by Neil Jordan, The Crying Game was
hailed as one of the best films of 1992, but

00:01:25.341 --> 00:01:29.310
in subsequent years, it's been overshadowed
by some of its cinematic cousins.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:32.730
That's a shame, because this moody thriller
has it all, from heart-wrenching romance to

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.170
hair-pulling tension.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:38.380
The film follows an IRA terrorist named Fergus
who befriends a British soldier, played by

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:46.680
Forest Whitaker.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.420
Unfortunately for their friendship, Fergus
is supposed to shoot the poor trooper.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.150
Whitaker's character asks Fergus to check
on his girlfriend after he's gone.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:59.030
Eventually Fergus leaves the IRA, travels
to London, and meets Dil, the soldier's girlfriend.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:02.990
He quickly falls for her, but that whole "I
shot your boyfriend" secret is always looming

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:03.990
in the background.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:08.030
It doesn't help matters that the IRA is busy
looking for Fergus, wanting to bring him back

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:09.030
to the fold.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.329
Honestly, there's a lot more going on in this
film than we can possibly say.

00:02:12.329 --> 00:02:16.239
So if you want to experience the entire emotional
experience then you'll definitely want to

00:02:16.239 --> 00:02:19.670
visit Netflix and try playing The Crying Game.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.319
Cartel Land

00:02:21.319 --> 00:02:25.730
Produced by Kathryn Bigelow and directed by
Matthew Heineman, Cartel Land is a visceral

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:29.459
thriller that feels a lot like The Hurt Locker
or Zero Dark Thirty.

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:32.299
The only difference is that Cartel Land is
a documentary.

00:02:32.299 --> 00:02:36.239
There are no actors, no script, just real-life
people armed to the teeth.

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:40.680
This white-knuckle 2015 thriller follows two
vigilante groups on opposite sides of the

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.280
border as they battle incredibly violent Mexican
cartels.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.849
We witness actual gunfights, real-life torture,
and one of the most harrowing car rides in

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:50.180
cinematic history.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:54.159
The movie also takes a nuanced look at the
issue, showing how vigilantes are fighting

00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:56.019
for their lives against gangs.

00:02:56.019 --> 00:03:00.019
On the other hand, these vigilante groups
have a tendency to go overboard, and over

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:03.900
on the American side, there's some horrible
racism fueling their efforts to hunt down

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.590
people who come across the border.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:10.389
"Why would you put two races in the same nation
and expect them to get along."

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:15.040
Cartel Land plunges viewers right into the
blood-and-guts-reality of the drug war, and

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.930
even though it's a documentary, it's as thrilling
as any fictional film you'll ever see.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.260
The Gift

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:25.449
Written and directed by Joel Edgerton, The
Gift is a creepy little suspense flick from

00:03:25.449 --> 00:03:29.709
2015 that will make you think twice when an
old friend calls and wants to catch up.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:34.450
The plot follows Simon and Robyn Callem, a
seemingly happy couple played by Jason Bateman

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:35.659
and Rebecca Hall.

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:38.840
They've gone through some trauma, but now
they're looking to start over in a new city,

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.900
in a new house, and with new lives.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:45.120
Unfortunately for the couple, Simon runs into
an old friend from school, a man named Gordo.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.520
"Gordo the weirdo."

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:49.800
"That's not very nice."

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:50.960
"Everybody had a name."

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:55.919
At first, Gordo just seems a little too eager
to please, but as strange gifts show up on

00:03:55.919 --> 00:03:59.590
the Callems' porch and tensions escalate,
it looks like Gordo might have more on his

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.140
mind than reminiscing about the good old days.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.230
That's just scratching the surface of the
story, and without saying much more about

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:09.959
the plot, The Gift is a tense and nasty little
movie with unsettling performances from its

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:15.629
three brilliant leads, not to mention an ending
that will likely leave you genuinely upset.

00:04:15.629 --> 00:04:17.209
A Patch of Fog

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:21.269
If you've seen Boardwalk Empire, then you
know Stephen Graham can be one intimidating

00:04:21.269 --> 00:04:25.020
dude, and he brings that same manic energy
to A Patch of Fog.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:30.110
In this atmospheric 2015 film, Game of Thrones'
Conleth Hill plays a famous author named Sandy

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:33.090
Duff who's living off the proceeds of a 20-year-old
book.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:37.500
When he's not giving lectures or appearing
on TV, he spends his spare time shoplifting,

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.561
which majorly backfires when he's caught by
a psycho security guard named Robert, played

00:04:41.561 --> 00:04:42.580
by Graham.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.980
However, Robert doesn't want to turn Sandy
over to the police.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.419
Robert just wants to be friends.

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:51.580
Obviously, when a super stalker wants to be
your buddy, that's never a good sign, and

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.520
their freaky friendship soon escalates to
a game of cat-and-mouse with some very serious

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:56.520
stakes.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.780
"You make it sound like I wanna stick pins
in ya."

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.639
"I just wanna be your friend."

00:05:05.639 --> 00:05:09.580
While we've seen similar stories before, the
highlight here is the tension between Graham

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.300
and Hill, both playing characters we empathize
with, even though we wouldn't necessarily

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.889
want to hang out with either one of them.

00:05:15.889 --> 00:05:17.870
Buster's Mal Heart

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:21.580
Thrillers don't come much stranger than 2016's
Buster's Mal Heart.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:25.690
Written and directed by Sarah Smith, the movie
finds Rami Malek playing a bearded mountain

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.440
man on the run from the cops.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:31.160
This outlaw hobo is named Buster, and when
he's not breaking into cabins, he's ranting

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.139
about an upcoming apocalypse he calls "The
Inversion."

00:05:34.139 --> 00:05:37.620
But how did Buster get to this place, with
gun-wielding cops on his trail?

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.220
Well, you'll start to find out as the film
jumps back to when Buster was a family man

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.220
named Jonah.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:47.289
Clean-shaven and suffocating, Jonah is a hotel
concierge who feels trapped by the system…until

00:05:47.289 --> 00:05:51.980
a conspiracy theorist shows up with wild ideas
about Y2K and robbing banks.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:56.259
Making all this even stranger, we occasionally
get glimpses of a third version of Malek,

00:05:56.259 --> 00:06:00.169
lost at sea, adding to the uneasy dream vibe
of the whole film.

00:06:00.169 --> 00:06:03.469
Buster's Mal Heart has some twists that will
keep you guessing, but ultimately, it's a

00:06:03.469 --> 00:06:07.450
mind-bending movie that will cause you to
praise Rami Malek's acting abilities while

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:10.569
questioning the nature of reality itself.

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:12.539
The Fury of a Patient Man

00:06:12.539 --> 00:06:17.099
Set in Madrid, The Fury of a Patient Man follows
a seemingly gentle man named Jose who falls

00:06:17.099 --> 00:06:19.020
in love with a lonely woman named Ana.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.569
Her husband, Luis, has been behind bars for
his part in a jewel heist, and of course,

00:06:22.569 --> 00:06:25.569
we all know things are going to get messy
when he's finally released.

00:06:25.569 --> 00:06:29.979
But just when you think you know where it's
going, the movie sets off in an entirely different

00:06:29.979 --> 00:06:30.979
direction.

00:06:30.979 --> 00:06:35.530
This brutal 2016 Spanish-language film features
some brilliantly suspenseful scenes, like

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:41.139
a tense moment in a boxing gym and a one-shot
car chase that ends in a terrific wreck.

00:06:41.139 --> 00:06:42.560
Bad Day for the Cut

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.210
Set in Northern Ireland, 2017's Bad Day for
the Cut is gory proof that you don't mess

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.220
with farmers, and you especially don't mess
with farmers' moms.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.610
This film focuses on a middle-aged man named
Donal, a farmer who's spent most of his life

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:56.219
taking care of his elderly mother.

00:06:56.219 --> 00:06:59.979
But his quiet existence is turned upside down
when she's killed after what seems to be a

00:06:59.979 --> 00:07:01.889
home invasion gone wrong.

00:07:01.889 --> 00:07:05.569
After joining forces with another victim,
Donal sets out to collect an eye for an eye,

00:07:05.569 --> 00:07:09.099
but he quickly realizes there are quite a
few secrets in his family tree.

00:07:09.099 --> 00:07:13.069
Still, that doesn't stop him from taking on
an army of bad guys to take revenge against

00:07:13.069 --> 00:07:15.800
the crime lord responsible for taking out
his mom.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:19.460
If you're a fan of crime flicks from the UK,
Bad Day for the Cut will definitely be a good

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.560
time on Netflix.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:23.290
Icarus

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:28.120
Directed by Bryan Fogel, 2017's Icarus picked
up the Oscar for Best Documentary at the 90th

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.300
Academy Awards.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:33.169
The film opens with Fogel wanting to explore
the world of performance enhancing drugs by

00:07:33.169 --> 00:07:37.210
injecting himself with all kinds of chemicals
before competing in a bike race.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:41.610
His little stunt soon leads him to Dr. Grigory
Rodchenkov, a colorful character and the man

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.840
in charge of Russia's anti-doping program.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:49.169
Soon, Rodchenkov is fearing for his life,
and we watch as he maneuvers around KGB agents,

00:07:49.169 --> 00:07:52.050
escapes the country, and faces the possibility
of assassination.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:56.539
A documentary that will have you on the edge
of your seat, Icarus is the perfect mix of

00:07:56.539 --> 00:07:59.870
informative storytelling and real-life thrills.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.330
Shimmer Lake

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:06.219
Sort of like Fargo crossed with Memento, Shimmer
Lake is a backwards story of bumbling criminals

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:08.029
who can't stop screwing up.

00:08:08.029 --> 00:08:12.819
Taking a page from the Christopher Nolan playbook,
this 2017 Netflix Original starts at the end

00:08:12.819 --> 00:08:16.789
and works its way toward the beginning, as
a group of small-town crooks plan and carry

00:08:16.789 --> 00:08:18.100
out a robbery.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:23.420
"Yeah Chris, it's going real good. Super good!"

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.700
Without a doubt, the highlight of the film
is Benjamin Walker as Zeke Sikes, a local

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.060
sheriff who walks softly, carries a big stick,
and is forced to deal with everything from

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.230
idiot FBI agents to a devious femme fatale.

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:40.090
Rainn Wilson is also great as Zeke's brother
Andy, a disgraced attorney who plays a key

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:41.820
role in the twisty plot.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:45.710
If you've seen James Gunn's Super, then you
know Wilson has impressive dramatic chops,

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.260
and he's pretty great here as a despicable,
desperate loser.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:50.480
"Where have I been?"

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:51.660
"Where have I been?

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:53.820
In a car, forever.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:54.820
A corn field.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:56.980
I spent the night in a junkyard."

00:08:56.980 --> 00:09:00.070
And if the backwards timeline sounds a bit
gimmicky, don't worry.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:03.650
It pays off beautifully, making Shimmer Lake
a dark tale that's totally worth unraveling.

